1: # Source-zero E-annulus: the exact component and normal deck
2: 
3: Working attachment record, 17 November 2026. The statements below concern
4: the actual E annulus and its chain charts. They supply boundary data; they
5: do not assert that the collision quotient and the cap have been attached
6: over the central collision point.
7: 
8: ## EA.1. The component permutation and its full-cycle representative
9: 
10: Use the notation and actual theta/Cartier maps of K39 Sections 19–22 and
11: 27. Thus (N=km), (n=\pm1), (c=nk), and the changed ordinary line
12: coordinate is (V_\eta). The positive (q_1)-deck, as an arrow on the
13: logarithmic base cover, is
14: \[
15:  S:(q_1\text{-sheet},V_\eta)\longmapsto
16:        (q_1\text{-sheet}+1,v^{-c}V_\eta).
17: \]
18: On the actual node charts
19: \[
20:  X_j=V_\eta/v^j,\qquad Y_j=v^{j+1}/V_\eta,
21:  \qquad X_jY_j=v,
22: \]
23: this is literally
24: \[
25:              S:(j,X_j,Y_j)\longmapsto(j-c,X_j,Y_j).       \tag{EA.1}
26: \]
27: Both normal coordinates are unchanged after the displayed index change.
28: This proves that the node components modulo the scalar period (N)
29: have (k) cycles of length (m), with the sign of (n) retained.
30: 
31: Write the full scalar period as
32: \[
33:  g:(Z,V_\eta)\longmapsto(g_ZZ,v^N g_0V_\eta).
34: \]
35: It sends chart (j) to chart (j+N), with
36: 
37: \[
38:         (Z,X_j,Y_j)\longmapsto(g_ZZ,g_0X_j,g_0^{-1}Y_j).
39: \]
40: After (m) positive (q_1)-deck arrows the index is (j-nN).
41: Returning to representative (j) by the *actual* period (g^n)
42: therefore gives the full-cycle arrow
43: \[
44:  C=g^nS^m:(Z,X,Y)\longmapsto
45:        (g_Z^nZ,g_0^nX,g_0^{-n}Y).                         \tag{EA.2}
46: \]
47: This is a forward-deck arrow on the chosen sheet. The
48: endpoint-to-initial closing in the associated mapping torus is its
49: inverse. No component reindexing has been discarded.
50: 
51: ## EA.2. The central source and normal maps
52: 
53: On (v=0), (0<|T|<\epsilon), the exact central identities already
54: proved from the chord and Cartier maps are
55: \[
56:  P^2Q=1,\qquad h=(Q,P^a),\qquad
57:  g_Z=P^{-b},\qquad g_0=2(-1)^{b+1}\lambda_0P.             \tag{EA.3}
58: \]
59: Here the factor (v^N) has been removed only in writing the node-chart
60: unit (g_0). The scalar in the actual suspension remains
61: 
62: \[
63:                          \lambda=v^N\lambda_0.
64: \]
65: For (a=1,b=2), (EA.2) has source multiplier (P^{-2n}=Q^n).
66: Dividing by the literal source period (h^n), whose line multiplier
67: is (P^n), gives
68: \[
69:  C_{\mathrm{good}}:(Z,X,Y)\longmapsto
70:        (Z,(-2\lambda_0)^nX,(-2\lambda_0)^{-n}Y).          \tag{EA.4}
71: \]
72: For (a=2,b=1), the actual central line is trivial on this punctured
73: annulus in the frame (ZV_\eta): its factor under (h) is
74: 
75: \[
76:                             QP^2=1.
77: \]
78: Accordingly put (\widehat X=ZX),
79: 
80: \[
81:  \widehat Y=Z^{-1}Y,\qquad \widehat X\widehat Y=v.
82: \]
83: Then the same arrow is
84: \[
85:  C_{\mathrm{red}}:(Z,\widehat X,\widehat Y)\longmapsto
86:        (P^{-n}Z,(2\lambda_0)^n\widehat X,
87:                          (2\lambda_0)^{-n}\widehat Y).   \tag{EA.5}
88: \]
89: The source multiplier (P^{-n}) is the marked nonzero two-torsion
90: translation. Its square is (P^{-2n}=Q^n), an actual source period.
91: It is not itself a source period: the already established asymptotics
92: 
93: \[
94:                P\sim16/T,\qquad Q\sim T^2/256
95: \]
96: give the half-period valuation. Thus the reduced full-cycle arrow retains
97: an actual source translation, even though its displayed normal units
98: are constant.
99: 
100: Equations (EA.4) and (EA.5) retain the full central units, not only their
101: winding numbers. In particular the positive-weight normal determinant
102: gets the unit (c/\bar c) for the displayed constant (c), after
103: conjugating the negative-weight coordinate. This statement does not
104: choose a logarithm across (T=0).
105: 
106: ## EA.3. The Cartier class and the remaining cap comparison
107: 
108: The flat frame (ZV_\eta) in (EA.5) is used only on the punctured
109: annulus. The source calculation of K39 Section 2 identifies the full
110: central Cartier line for (a=2) with (O(C_0)), and for (a=1)
111: with (O(G_0-O)), whose component degrees on ((C_0,C_1)) are
112: 
113: \[
114:                           (-1,+1).
115: \]
116: Consequently the punctured trivialization in (EA.5) is not declared to
117: extend as a nowhere-zero section across the (I_2) fibre. The vertical
118: Cartier divisor remains part of the attachment.
119: 
120: The finite cap has the actual generator
121: 
122: \[
123:  A=v^{kn}r_0^nA_0,\qquad A_0^m=B_0^n,
124: \]
125: and the ordinary-to-cap map is the full (F_0) fixed in RCZ.5–7,
126: after the explicitly displayed changed origins. It identifies the
127: forward (q_1)-deck with the inverse cap-root arrow, including the
128: source translation and the line character. It therefore transports
129: (EA.2) to the cap frame with its full source/line cocycle. No assertion
130: that this transported frame extends across (T=0) follows from the
131: constant normal units in (EA.4)–(EA.5).
132: 
133: For the good branch, the chosen division representative
134: 
135: \[
136:  R=(QP^2)^{1/m}
137: \]
138: and the identity-component representative (R_I=P^{2/m}) on a strict
139: I chart differ by (Q^{1/m}). Their (m)-norms differ by the source
140: period (Q), including its actual line factor (P). The alternative
141: strict-I representative has no component translation there, but using
142: it in the cap requires an actual affine source conjugacy and its line
143: lift, with the integral annular cochain carried. The finite-cap
144: equation to solve is the explicit one from AE.1–4:
145: 
146: \[
147:                        (1-D)T=Z,
148: \]
149: where (Z) is the exact difference of the two affine translation
150: terms and has zero *cyclic* norm. A pointwise (m)-division identity
151: alone does not establish that cyclic-norm condition. This is the next
152: comparison being computed, and no global filling or numerical return
153: is assigned in this record.
154: 
155: The finite exact certificate is
156: \path{code/part3_fourfold/source_zero_e_annular_deck.py}; it checks both
157: signs, the component cycles, the full-period reindexing and the two
158: central normal-unit cancellations.
159: 
160: ## EA.4. The primitive chamber map on the actual finite cap
161: 
162: Here the primitive map is the *negative* source translation of SZ.7:
163: 
164: \[
165:  U_1:(p,w)\longmapsto(p-G,w/X(p-G)).
166: \]
167: For (a=2), retain the actual Cartier map
168: 
169: \[
170:  r(p)=X(p-G),\qquad
171:  r:O(2G-O)\longrightarrow O(G-O)^{\otimes2}.
172: \]
173: The primitive map in the original line is therefore
174: 
175: \[
176:  U_2^{\rm Cartier}=r_{\rm target}^{-1}
177:               U_2^{\rm tensor}r_{\rm source}.            \tag{EA.6}
178: \]
179: It is (EA.6), rather than an unlabelled tensor-power frame, that is
180: carried to the cap. In the common Cox coordinates of SZ.14–15 every
181: 
182: \[
183:                          U_a: \text{t-ruling}\longrightarrow
184:                                       \text{s-ruling}
185: \]
186: is the identity on the common nonzero coordinate (V). This is the
187: inverse direction to K23's s-ruling-to-t-ruling map
188: 
189: \[
190:                  \tau(h,q_H)=(q_H^{-1}h q_H,q_H).
191: \]
192: The degree-two case retains the actual residual (\mu_2) and line
193: charge two.
194: 
195: Write (q_\infty=z^m) on the cap and
196: 
197: \[
198:  q=q_\infty^{-1}h,qquad h=1-T_0(v)q_\infty.
199: \]
200: There is the following literal normalization of the primitive lift:
201: 
202: \[
203:   U_{\rm cap}=z^{-ma/2}U_a^{\rm Cartier},qquad
204:   B=2(-1)^{b+1}\lambda h\,U_{\rm cap}^{,b},qquad ab=2.
205:                                                                \tag{EA.7}
206: \]
207: The exponent (ma/2) is an integer in each admitted branch. To
208: verify the extending map, first take the good branch (m=4p,a=1).
209: The actual root coordinates have (X=z^{-2p}X'). Thus the primitive
210: target multiplier (1/X) is exactly (z^{2p}/X'). The root map
211: 
212: \[
213:         (p,w)\longmapsto(p-G',w/X'(p-G'))
214: \]
215: is an extending isomorphism of the actual degree-zero root line:
216: its horizontal divisor is the same Cartier identity as SZ.7, and at
217: the smooth central root fibre its generic coefficient is a nonzero
218: unit, so its possible whole-fibre divisor has coefficient zero.
219: This proves the first equality of (EA.7) in the good branch.
220: 
221: For the reduced branch (b=1,a=2), use (EA.6) before passing to the
222: actual corrected root line. The already constructed root suspension
223: is an everywhere invertible map (B_0); its full coefficient in
224: SZ.12 is retained. Since (h) is an extending nonzero unit,
225: 
226: \[
227:                         U_{\rm cap}=B_0/(2h)              \tag{EA.8}
228: \]
229: is an extending source/line map. Comparing with the exact ordinary
230: identity (B_0=2qU_2^{\rm Cartier}) gives
231: 
232: \[
233:                         U_{\rm cap}=z^{-m}U_2^{\rm Cartier}.
234: \]
235: This is the reduced equality in (EA.7). It incorporates the Cartier
236: correction of the reduced III source; the raw coefficient
237: 
238: \[
239:                        z^{-4p}/X'(p-G')^2
240: \]
241: on an uncorrected tensor frame is not used as its extension.
242: Finally (z^{mab/2}=z^m=q_\infty), so multiplying by the actual
243: selected factor (q) proves the second equality of (EA.7) with the
244: unit (h), rather than with a discarded base power.
245: 
246: The actual finite character is also determined. On the good root the
247: canonical deck sends (X'\) to (-X'), and preserves the marked
248: source divisor. Consequently
249: 
250: \[
251:  D U_{\rm cap}D^{-1}=-U_{\rm cap}.
252: \]
253: The translation lift in (A_0) commutes with (U_{\rm cap}) by the
254: literal constant-factor presentation of a degree-zero elliptic line.
255: The equality extends over the root line. Hence
256: 
257: \[
258:               U_{\rm cap}A_0U_{\rm cap}^{-1}=-A_0
259:                     \quad (a,b)=(1,2).                   \tag{EA.9}
260: \]
261: Equivalently the first primitive step carries the finite delta
262: character (d\) to (d+m/2); the second returns to (d).
263: On the reduced cap, (EA.8), the exact norm relation and the
264: deck-invariance of (h) instead give
265: 
266: \[
267:                  U_{\rm cap}A_0=A_0U_{\rm cap}
268:                     \quad (a,b)=(2,1).                   \tag{EA.10}
269: \]
270: Both statements retain (n=\pm1) and every original finite delta
271: character. Multiplication of (A_0) by the rescaled parameter factor
272: 
273: \[
274:                               v^{kn}r_0^n
275: \]
276: does not change either commutator.
277: 
278: On the chosen root sheet the full annular Cartier map carries
279: 
280: \[
281:             U_a^{\rm Cartier}\longmapsto z^{ma/2}U_{\rm cap}.
282: \]
283: Its root-deck character cancels exactly: in the good branch both
284: 
285: \[
286:                          \zeta_m^{ma/2}quad\text{and}quad -1
287: \]
288: are (-1), and in the reduced branch both characters are (1).
289: The translation part of the full (F_0) commutes with the displayed
290: primitive lift in the actual degree-zero-line group. Thus this is a
291: literal annular comparison with the full root/line map, not only a
292: comparison of source points. After (b) steps it is exactly the
293: actual suspension in (EA.7).
294: 
295: In particular, in the reduced branch the forward suspension retains
296: one t-ruling-to-s-ruling arrow; the cap inserts no second ruling
297: change. The inverse suspension has the opposite arrow. The
298: identification of this arrow with the oriented residual stable end of
299: the real collision bordism is still a separate map. No characteristic
300: number is inferred here solely from the number of primitive factors.
